  "query_preview": "..\nThe main focus over the next few days will be the remnants of Invest\n(94W/95W...as 95W was re-designated today by JTWC after 94W was\ncancelled yesterday). This feature will be decaying as it heads up\nthis way, but sufficient lift via elevated remnant vorticity centers\nand deep moisture advection will increase rainfall potential from\nsouth to north starting Saturday, persisting through the remainder of\nthe weekend. Modest omegas are seen in the time height series\nsuggesting a few claps of thunder can't be ruled out either,as PWATs\n(Precipitable Water Values) climb from current values near 1.5 inches\nto 2.3 inches over the weekend. Then, as we head towards the middle\nof next week, drier conditions will return to the region.",
